-# Low-level bindings for PROJ v9.6.x
+# Low-level bindings for PROJ v9.9.x
+
+This vendored tree is a path fork of `proj-sys` 0.27.0. Its fork-specific
+change replaces upstream system/dynamic libtiff and pkg-config linking with
+statically linked vendored libtiff and zlib.
+
+The libtiff source is the full upstream `v4.7.2` tree at commit
+`d01a94be176f5f6a87f7ee1c0b32e65416aa2b4d`, recorded in
+`../libtiff/libtiff.pin`. Initialize it before building from a fresh
+checkout:
+
+```sh
+git submodule update --init vendor/libtiff/source
+```
+
+The bundled build verifies the pinned PROJ 9.9.0 archive and applies the
+reviewed exact-meaning CRS edits by unique source anchors. A changed archive,
+version, or upstream source layout fails the build instead of silently
+changing CRS axis, unit, datum, or conversion semantics.
+
+Builds do not fetch source or transformation grids from the network. The
+`tiff` feature enables user-supplied PROJ GeoTIFF transformation grids; it is
+not a gometry raster API.
+
+Gometry's bundled target also contains a private 9.9.0 context constructor. It
+starts from PROJ's native defaults instead of cloning the process default, so
+the gometry CRS layer does not need a per-context `proj.ini`. The constructor
+is deliberately unavailable to system/pkg-config builds.
 
 **This is a
 [`*-sys`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/build-scripts.html#-sys-packages)
 crate; you shouldn't use its API directly.** See the
 [`proj`](https://github.com/georust/proj) crate for general use.
@@ -16,18 +43,17 @@ If an acceptable installation is not found, proj-sys will attempt to build
 libproj from source bundled in the crate.
 
 ## Features
 
 - `bundled_proj` - forces building libproj from source even if an acceptable
-  version could be found on your system.  Note that SQLite3 must be
-  present on your system if you wish to use this feature, and that it builds
-  `libproj` **without** its native network functionality; you will have to
-  implement your own set of callbacks if you wish to make use of them (see the
-[`proj`](https://crates.io/crates/proj) crate for an example).
-- `bundled_proj_tiff` - If the `bundled_proj` feature is enabled, adding the
-  `bundled_proj_tiff` feature will build PROJ with TIFF support. Note that
-  libtiff must be present on your system if you wish to use this feature.
+  version could be found on your system. It also enables bundled SQLite and
+  builds `libproj` **without** its native network functionality; you will have
+  to implement your own set of callbacks if you wish to make use of them (see
+  the [`proj`](https://crates.io/crates/proj) crate for an example).
+- `tiff` - enables PROJ TIFF support and links the path dependency's statically
+  bundled libtiff and zlib. No system libtiff is used, and builds do not fetch
+  source or transformation grids from the network.
 
